## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scheduler that balances SLA guarantees with cost efficiency in a multi-tenant, cross-region LLM-ops environment.

## Key Concepts

- Quality of Service with per-tenant quotas and budgets
- Preemption mechanisms and priority queue management
- Cost modeling and real-time optimization dashboards
- Regional routing strategies and data locality considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: token-bucket burst control
function canSubmit(tenant) {
  const bucket = tenants[tenant];
  if (bucket.tokens > 0) {
    bucket.tokens--;
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design SLA-aware routing with multi-tenant fairness, regulatory constraints, and cost.

## Key Concepts
- SLA/QoS, model pools, edge vs cloud, real-time routing, circuit breakers, fault isolation, observability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for routing decision
function route(request, tenancy, pools, metrics) {
  const budget = tenancy.latencyBudget;
  const eta = estimateETA(request, pools, metrics);
  const chosen = (eta <= budget) ? selectPool(pools, tenancy) : escalateFallback(tenancy);
  return chosen;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test burst traffic and backpressure across tenants?
- How would you validate data locality guarantees under failover?

## Why This Is Asked
