## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical data provenance and tamper detection in multi-tenant LLM gateways.

## Key Concepts
- Data provenance and tamper-evident logging
- Per-tenant keys and HMAC signing
- Privacy-aware logging and redaction
- Simple retention and rotation policies

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function signLogLine(line, key){
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key);
  h.update(line);
  return h.digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate tenant keys without breaking logs?
- How would you prove log integrity to auditors without exposing PII?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess practical understanding of per-tenant routing and SLA management in LLM-ops, focusing on simple guards and deterministic fallbacks rather than abstract theory.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant routing and policy application
- Latency budgeting and model selection
- Deterministic fallback behavior

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple routing sketch
function selectModel(tenant, latencyMs) {
  const budget = tenant.budgetMs;
  if (latencyMs <= budget * 0.8) return 'small';
  if (latencyMs <= budget) return 'default';
  return 'large';
}
```

